# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Env file hierarchy (Next.js / Node convention)
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#
# This file (.env.example)        committed.       Documents required vars. NO SECRETS.
# .env                             gitignored.     Non-secret local defaults.
# .env.local                       gitignored.     **Local secrets go HERE.** Per-machine.
# .env.development.local           gitignored.     Local overrides for `next dev`.
# .env.production.local            gitignored.     Local overrides for `next start` (rare).
#
# Production / preview deployments: secrets are injected by Vercel / AWS Amplify
# at build & runtime — they are NOT read from any .env file in the repo.
#   Vercel:  Project Settings → Environment Variables
#   Amplify: App → Hosting → Environment Variables
# The `amplify.yml` build phase writes scoped vars from the Amplify env scope to
# `apps/web/.env.production` at build time, keyed by this `.env.example` file.
#
# Per-app envs live in apps/*/.env.example. This root file is referenced by
# `turbo.json` globalDependencies so changes bust the build cache appropriately.
#
# Pre-commit hook: gitleaks scans the staged index. If you accidentally stage a
# credential (AWS key, GitHub token, Stripe key, etc.), the commit is rejected.
# It is the same binary and ruleset CI runs — see AGENTS.md, "Secrets".

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Database
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#
# The dev container runs PostgreSQL as a sidecar (.devcontainer/docker-compose.yml).
# It is already up when your terminal opens — nothing to start by hand.
#
# The value below is the LOCAL one and is safe to commit: the database is bound
# to 127.0.0.1, holds nothing real, and is rebuilt from migrations. Copy it into
# `.env` (gitignored) or leave it here; do NOT put a hosted credential in this
# file — that belongs in `.env.local`, which is gitignored.
#
# From INSIDE the dev container, the host is `db` — the compose service name.
# From your own machine (a GUI client on the host), it is `localhost:5432`.
#
# Why the path ends in `/postgres`: that is the database name, and it matches
# what Supabase gives you, so moving to hosted changes only the host and
# password — not the connection-string shape, your migrations, or a dump.
#   Supabase: postgresql://postgres:<pw>@db.<ref>.supabase.co:5432/postgres
DATABASE_URL=postgresql://postgres:postgres@db:5432/postgres

# Browse it at http://localhost:8080 (Adminer, also a sidecar). Server `db`,
# username `postgres`, password `postgres`, database `postgres`.
